{title: Joy To The World}
{artist: Isaac Watts}
{composer: George Frideric Handel}
{key: G}
{time: 2/4}
{tempo: 110}
{tags: Christmas, Worship, Traditional}
{copyright: Public Domain}

{comment: A joyful Christmas hymn based on Psalm 98}

{start_of_verse}
[G]Joy to the world, the [D]Lord is [G]come
Let [C]Earth rec[D]eive her [G]King
Let [G]every heart prepare Him room
And [G]Heaven and nature sing
And [D]Heaven and nature sing
And [Em]Heaven, and [C]Heaven, and [D]nature [G]sing
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
[G]Joy to the earth, the [D]Savior [G]reigns
Let [C]men their [D]songs emp[G]loy
While [G]fields and floods, rocks, hills and plains
Re[G]peat the sounding joy
Re[D]peat the sounding joy
Re[Em]peat, re[C]peat the [D]sounding [G]joy
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
[G]He rules the world with [D]truth and [G]grace
And [C]makes the [D]nations [G]prove
The [G]glories of His righteousness
And [G]wonders of His love
And [D]wonders of His love
And [Em]wonders, [C]wonders, [D]of His [G]love
{end_of_verse}
